<title>CHINA: China first-half crude oil imports up 33 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>China first-half crude oil imports up 33 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>China imported 14.42 million tonnes of crude oil in the first half, up 33 percent compared with the year-ago period, the International Business Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>China's imports of oil products soared 71 percent year-on-year to 11.76 million tonnes in the first six months, the newspaper quoted customs figures as showing. It gave no details of oil product imports.</p>
<p>China's exports of crude oil reached 10.23 million tonnes in the first half, a rise of 20 percent from the same period last year, it said.</p>
<p>The newspaper did not give figures for June alone.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
